# Security and build rules

- Never commit API keys, tokens, or secrets to the repository
- Keep secrets out of the build: ScriptableObjects, Resources, and StreamingAssets ship inside the player and can be extracted. Fetch secrets from your backend at runtime; keep editor-only credentials in environment variables or `EditorUserSettings`
- Strip debug symbols and logging in release builds
- Use IL2CPP for release builds (harder to reverse engineer than Mono, which ships readable IL)
- Enable code stripping to reduce build size
- Encrypt sensitive save data; never store plaintext passwords
- Validate server-side in multiplayer; never trust client data
- Use `Debug.unityLogger.logEnabled = false` in production or wrap in #if UNITY_EDITOR
- Obfuscate sensitive strings if targeting platforms where decompilation is a risk
- Install third-party packages only from sources you trust, pin their versions in `Packages/manifest.json`, and review updates before accepting them
